---
alwaysApply: true
description: DOM capture and style extraction rules
---

# DOM Capture Rules

Element capture must produce a portable snippet.

---

# Capture Process

Steps:

1. detect clicked element
2. clone subtree
3. traverse DOM
4. extract computed styles
5. inline styles
6. remove external assets

---

# Inline Style Rules

Only include visual styles:

```

display
position
margin
padding
font
color
background
border
flex
grid

```

Omit default values (e.g. `position: static`, `margin: 0`, `opacity: 1`) for conciseness.

Ignore:

```

transition
animation
cursor
pointer-events

```

---

# Asset Handling

Replace with placeholders:

```

video
canvas
iframe

```

Inline SVGs: preserve when cloning. Use `createElementNS` with SVG namespace for SVG elements and descendants so they render correctly. SVG sprite references (`<use href="...">`) rely on base URL resolution in preview; same-origin sprites load when sourceUrl is set.

---

# Script Removal

Remove:

```

script
iframe
tracking pixels

```

---

# Output HTML

Output must be:

```

clean
portable
framework neutral

```

---

# Export Formats

Generate:

```

HTML
JSX

```

JSX must convert style syntax correctly.
```